IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgi-contracts-seal`

-- Tests for sgi-contracts-seal.l4 (ss 41 to 42A). Expected values are written from the text beside each assertion.

§ `s 41(1) and (2)`

-- Arguments: purports to be entered into before formation; the company has been formed.
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the contract or transaction may be ratified by the company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the contract or transaction may be ratified by the company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the contract or transaction may be ratified by the company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: purports to be entered into before formation; the company has ratified it.
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the company is bound by and entitled to the benefit of the contract or transaction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the company is bound by and entitled to the benefit of the contract or transaction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41(1) the company is bound by and entitled to the benefit of the contract or transaction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): arguments: the person purported to act for the company; the company has ratified; express agreement to the contrary.
#ASSERT `s 41(2) the person is personally bound by the contract or transaction and entitled to the benefit of it` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(2) the person is personally bound by the contract or transaction and entitled to the benefit of it` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(2) the person is personally bound by the contract or transaction and entitled to the benefit of it` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(2) the person is personally bound by the contract or transaction and entitled to the benefit of it` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 41(3) to (9)`

-- (3): each form paired with its way is permitted; any other pairing is not addressed.
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the contract may be made on behalf of the corporation in the way` `s 41(3)(a) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be required to be in writing under seal` `s 41(3)(a) in writing under the common seal of the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the contract may be made on behalf of the corporation in the way` `s 41(3)(b) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be required to be in writing signed by the parties to be charged` `s 41(3)(b) in writing signed by a person acting under the authority, express or implied, of the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the contract may be made on behalf of the corporation in the way` `s 41(3)(c) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be valid although made by parol only` `s 41(3)(c) by parol by a person acting under the authority, express or implied, of the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the contract may be made on behalf of the corporation in the way` `s 41(3)(a) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be required to be in writing under seal` `s 41(3)(c) by parol by a person acting under the authority, express or implied, of the corporation` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the contract may be made on behalf of the corporation in the way` `s 41(3)(b) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be required to be in writing signed by the parties to be charged` `s 41(3)(a) in writing under the common seal of the corporation` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the contract may be made on behalf of the corporation in the way` `s 41(3)(c) a contract which if made between private persons would by law be valid although made by parol only` `s 41(3) another way` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the contract may be made on behalf of the corporation in the way` `s 41(3) another contract` `s 41(3)(a) in writing under the common seal of the corporation` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the contract is effectual in law and binds the corporation and its successors and all other parties` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the contract is effectual in law and binds the corporation and its successors and all other parties` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the contract may be varied or discharged` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the contract may be varied or discharged` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(3) the contract may be varied or discharged` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4).
#ASSERT `s 41(4) the document or proceeding may be signed by an authorised officer of the corporation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(4) the document or proceeding may be signed by an authorised officer of the corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(4) the document or proceeding may be signed by an authorised officer of the corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(4) the document or proceeding needs to be under the common seal` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41(4) the document or proceeding needs to be under the common seal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5).
#ASSERT `s 41(5) the corporation may empower the person as its agent or attorney to execute deeds on its behalf` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(5) the corporation may empower the person as its agent or attorney to execute deeds on its behalf` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: empowered under the common seal; signed under the agent's seal; signed under the official seal; the official seal is one subsection (7) allows.
#ASSERT `s 41(5) the deed binds the corporation and has the same effect as if it were under its common seal` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(5) the deed binds the corporation and has the same effect as if it were under its common seal` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(5) the deed binds the corporation and has the same effect as if it were under its common seal` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(5) the deed binds the corporation and has the same effect as if it were under its common seal` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(5) the deed binds the corporation and has the same effect as if it were under its common seal` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6): arguments: the instrument mentions a period; its last day; notice has been given to the person dealing; the day it was given; the date asked.
#ASSERT `s 41(6) the authority of the agent or attorney continues as between the corporation and the person dealing with the agent or attorney` TRUE (Date 31 12 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(6) the authority of the agent or attorney continues as between the corporation and the person dealing with the agent or attorney` TRUE (Date 31 12 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No period mentioned: until notice of the revocation or determination has been given to the person dealing.
#ASSERT `s 41(6) the authority of the agent or attorney continues as between the corporation and the person dealing with the agent or attorney` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(6) the authority of the agent or attorney continues as between the corporation and the person dealing with the agent or attorney` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(6) the authority of the agent or attorney continues as between the corporation and the person dealing with the agent or attorney` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (7).
#ASSERT `s 41(7) the corporation may have for use in a place outside Singapore an official seal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(7) the corporation may have for use in a place outside Singapore an official seal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(7) the corporation may have for use in a place outside Singapore an official seal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(7) the official seal is as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(7) the official seal is as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41(7) the official seal is as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41(7) the person affixing the official seal has certified the date and the place` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(7) the person affixing the official seal has certified the date and the place` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(7) the person affixing the official seal has certified the date and the place` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The certificate has no time limit, so no trace reaches BREACH. The act done: FULFILLED. No act: the duty stands (RESIDUAL).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 41(7) the person affixing the official seal must certify the date and the place` "Ali" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Ali" DOES `s 41(7) certify in writing under his or her hand, on the instrument to which the official seal is affixed, the date on which and the place at which it is affixed` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 41(7) the person affixing the official seal must certify the date and the place` "Ali" AT 0 WITH
-- (8): arguments: the authority is not under seal; it is valid by the law of the country of incorporation; the instrument was executed by the donee or agent; the purpose is to be effected in Singapore.
#ASSERT `s 41(8) the instrument under seal is as valid as if the authority had been under seal` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(8) the instrument under seal is as valid as if the authority had been under seal` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(8) the instrument under seal is as valid as if the authority had been under seal` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(8) the instrument under seal is as valid as if the authority had been under seal` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(8) the instrument under seal is as valid as if the authority had been under seal` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (9): arguments: executed by a donee or agent whose authority was not under seal; the day it was executed.
#ASSERT `s 41(9) subsection (8) applies to the instrument` TRUE (Date 14 5 1987) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(9) subsection (8) applies to the instrument` TRUE (Date 15 5 1987) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(9) subsection (8) applies to the instrument` FALSE (Date 14 5 1987) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 41A to 41C`

#ASSERT `s 41A(1) the company may have a common seal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41A(1) the company may have a common seal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41A(1) the company needs to have a common seal` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41A(1) the company needs to have a common seal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 41A(2): the answer is the same whether or not the company has a common seal.
#ASSERT `s 41A(2) sections 41B and 41C apply to the company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41A(2) sections 41B and 41C apply to the company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41A(2) sections 41B and 41C apply to the company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 41B(1): arguments: a deed; the number of directors who sign; a secretary signs; a director signs before an attesting witness.
#ASSERT `s 41B(1) the company may execute the document without affixing a common seal` TRUE 1 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41B(1) the company may execute the document without affixing a common seal` TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41B(1) the company may execute the document without affixing a common seal` TRUE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41B(1) the company may execute the document without affixing a common seal` TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41B(1) the company may execute the document without affixing a common seal` TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41B(1) the company may execute the document without affixing a common seal` FALSE 2 TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 41B(2) to (4).
#ASSERT `s 41B(2) the document has the same effect as if it were executed under the common seal of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41B(2) the document has the same effect as if it were executed under the common seal of the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41B(3) the document is considered to be signed by the person for the purposes of subsection (1) or (2)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 41B(3) the document is considered to be signed by the person for the purposes of subsection (1) or (2)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41B(3) the document is considered to be signed by the person for the purposes of subsection (1) or (2)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41B(4) section 41B applies to the document` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41B(4) section 41B applies to the document` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 41C: arguments: a law requires the seal or provides consequences; signed as 41B(1)(a), (b) or (c); signed as 41B(3).
#ASSERT `s 41C the document satisfies the written law or rule of law` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41C the document satisfies the written law or rule of law` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41C the document satisfies the written law or rule of law` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41C the document satisfies the written law or rule of law` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 42A`

#ASSERT `s 42A(1) section 42A applies to the company or foreign company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42A(1) section 42A applies to the company or foreign company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42A(1) section 42A applies to the company or foreign company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42A(2) the company or foreign company is deemed to be used for purposes prejudicial to public welfare` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42A(2) the company or foreign company is deemed to be used for purposes prejudicial to public welfare` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42A(2) the company or foreign company is deemed to be used for purposes prejudicial to public welfare` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42A(2) the company may be liable to be wound up by the Court under section 125(1)(n) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42A(2) the company may be liable to be wound up by the Court under section 125(1)(n) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42A(2) the foreign company may be liable to have its name struck off the register by the Registrar under section 377(8)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42A(2) the foreign company may be liable to have its name struck off the register by the Registrar under section 377(8)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 42A(3) "charitable purpose" the purpose or object is a charitable purpose` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42A(3) "charitable purpose" the purpose or object is a charitable purpose` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 42A(3) "charitable purpose" the purpose or object is a charitable purpose` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
